PRIMARY QUIET-BOTTLENECK RESULT
The quiet buffer looks:

uninteresting
to:
variance

and

weakly related
to:
ordinary correlation.

But:
causally perturbing it
removes:

approximately 12.5%
of the future recovery-plan fraction.

Thus:

LOW VARIANCE
DOES NOT MEAN
LOW VIABILITY IMPORTANCE.

